8,(PDF) Rhythm and the Synthetic Drift of Munda,https://www.academia.edu/78958260/Rhythm_and_the_Synthetic_Drift_of_Munda,The text explores the linguistic divergence between Munda and Mon-Khmer languages within the Austroasiatic family. Munda has shifted from head-first to head-last syntax due to a historical change in rhythmic patterns.,Munda,Austro-Asiatic
9,Munda People: Ancient Austro-Asiatic Tribe of... - Native Tribe Info,https://nativetribe.info/munda-people-ancient-austro-asiatic-tribe-of-eastern-india/,"Their languages, a branch of Austro-Asiatic, offer valuable clues about their ancient origins and migrations. Their languages, while diverse, share common linguistic roots, demonstrating a shared ancestry.",Munda,Austro-Asiatic
